import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.route.RouteLocator;
import org.springframework.cloud.gateway.route.builder.RouteLocatorBuilder;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;

@Configuration
public class ApiGatewayConfig {

    @Bean
    public RouteLocator customRouteLocator(RouteLocatorBuilder builder) {
        return builder.routes()
            .route("auth-service", r -> r.path("/auth/**")
                .filters(f -> f.stripPrefix(1).reqRateLimiter(c -> c.setReplenishRate(5).setBurstCapacity(10)))
                .uri("http://auth-service"))
            .route("content-delivery", r -> r.path("/cdn/**")
                .filters(f -> f.circuitBreaker(c -> c.setName("myCircuitBreaker").setFailureRateThreshold(30)))
                .uri("http://cdn-service"))
            .route("transaction-processing", r -> r.path("/transactions/**")
                .filters(f -> f.rewritePath("/transactions/(?<segment>.*?)/**", "/${segment}/**"))
                .uri("http://transaction-service"))
            .build();
    }
}
```

This Java code snippet demonstrates the configuration of an API gateway using Spring Cloud Gateway. The `RouteLocator` bean defines different routes for handling requests to authentication, content delivery, and transaction processing services. Each route includes specific filters to implement dynamic rate limiting, circuit breaking, and path rewriting.

Rate limiting is applied to the `/auth/**` path using the `reqRateLimiter` filter with custom settings for replenish rate and burst capacity. Circuit breaking is configured for the `/cdn/**` path using the `circuitBreaker` filter with a failure rate threshold. Path rewriting is used in the `/transactions/**` route to modify the request URI dynamically.

This example provides a basic structure for implementing an adaptive, resilient, and extensible API gateway that meets the specified requirements of handling diverse service requests, integrating with third-party APIs and databases, managing system dependencies, and optimizing performance under varying conditions.']

